lisa-design:
- Root cause (from T4's own output, "unable to resolve host ws-tskfactory-warm-build", and systemd v255's hostname_cleanup): nerdctl's /etc/hosts maps the workspace name ws-tsk_<id>, but systemd (PID 1 in the guest) re-sets the hostname from /etc/hostname with '_' dropped, so the kernel hostname ws-tsk<id> is mapped by nothing. The kata hosts file itself is fine (the createRuntime hook runs before runtime-rs shares /etc/hosts, per the shim's journal).
- Fix in the image, not the helper: libnss-myhostname with "hosts: files myhostname dns". Resolves whatever hostname systemd picks, no DNS, no write to /etc/hosts (the guest's /etc/hosts is the host's nerdctl file shared read-only through virtio-fs), no helper protocol bump or sudo reinstall; the image is rebuilt by host init anyway (contextSHA256).
- Rejected: helper --hostname with '_' -> '-' (exact root fix, but protocol 7 and a sudo reinstall, which the spec asked to avoid); a 127.0.1.1 line written at boot (would replicate systemd's cleanup in sh, or race the first sudo from a unit, and /etc/hosts isn't writable from the guest).
- The package's postinst appends myhostname after dns; the RUN rewrites the line and greps it, so the build fails if Ubuntu changes the default.
- The new RUN is its own layer after base.sh's so BuildKit keeps base.sh's layer cached.
- Tart is not changed: tart never passes the workspace name as the guest's hostname (the guest keeps the base image's), so the '_' cause can't arise there.
